WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.360
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.360
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Nightingale</b>

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Budding Crimson</b>

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Flowing</b>

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.780
What would you like?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.000
Otousan!

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.160
Has Itsuka come home yet?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.440
Not yet.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.500
I wonder if she's at the train station again?

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.860
P-Papa!

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:57.700
Wh—

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.120
Who are you?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.910
That's what I'd like to ask.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.560
Huh? What?!

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.820
I'm getting on! I'm getting on!

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.580
<i>It wasn't him this time, either.</i>

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:33.860
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:56.070 --> 00:03:02.450
<b>Nagomu and Itsuka</b>

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.380
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.380
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.390
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.390
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.990
It's been ten years.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.760
Thank you! Next, we have the heartthrob
 band you've all been waiting for...

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.720
Chestnut Manju!

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.800
Good evening!

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.110
Man... I'm sure the audience 
must've been really tired!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.120
<b>Chestnut</b>

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.120
<b>Chestnut</b>

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.120
I mean, we were up after a 
string of hard rock bands.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.490
Should we just go have a great time drinking?

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.010
Sorry, Nagomu.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:50.570
Huh?

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:52.620
We're out.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.440
What was that? All of them together...

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.150
The members have changed, but we've 
been doing this for ten years, right?

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.320
Should be no surprise this 
has got me feeling gloomy...

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.480
Thanks.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.640
From my mom?

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.650
This is...

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.650
It's our, Ryokushou's, sakura manju!

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.810
This color combination, aroma, mouthfeel...

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.700
and the perfect level of sweetness!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.140
So yummy!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:29.370
<b>Gloom</b>

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:31.160
All my gloomy feelings... 
They've been exorcised!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.500
Huh? A letter?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.310
What's with that?

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.000
Usually, New Year's cards are 
the only things we exchange.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.200
Dad?!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:46.590
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:46.590
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.380
Well, then, I'm going to go run deliveries!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.110
I'm home!

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.990
It's... been... a while...

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:11.700
How dare you come in here 
acting so pointlessly cheerful.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:14.710
Yo—

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.960
Yo?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.490
You're totally healthy!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.960
<b>I
N
 
M
E
M
O
R
I
A
M
 
K
O
U
T
O
K
U</b>

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.450
Grandpa, it's been a while. I came home.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.390
Honestly.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.900
You haven't been back since you ran out, 
talking about what you wanted to do.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.010
After all this time, what did
 you come back for?

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.620
To carry on this shop.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.690
Some amateur who's wandered for ten years,

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.790
never even touching wagashi, 
is saying what now?

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:43.210
When I heard you'd been hospitalized,
 it really hit me...

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.320
I wondered who was gonna
 take care of this shop.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.120
On my way here, I thought 
about all kinds of illnesses...

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.360
But I never imagined...

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.720
that it would be hemorrhoids!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.630
But, to think you'd be so worried 
you'd come all the way home.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.580
We're delighted, aren't we, Otousan?

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.840
I can't rely on you. I've already 
got someone to inherit the shop.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.440
This manju is yummy!

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.810
Isn't it? We kneaded salt-preserved 
sakura into the outer layer.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:11.500
That's not what we're 
talking about right now!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.100
Listen to me!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.530
I'm back.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.300
Oh, welcome home.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:16.930
Huh?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:17.600
Huh?

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:18.800
Huh?!

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.690
Perfect timing. Come sit here.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.420
What is it? Why are you 
staring at her like that?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.950
Oh, sorry. That was rude of me.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.960
It's just... at the station, I 
was mistaken for someone else.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.710
And I was thinking that she 
looks a lot like that girl.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:36.700
Mistaken for someone?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.520
That's right. She grabbed 
my arm and said, "Papa!"

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:43.180
Th-They say that everyone's got three 
other people who look just like them!

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.630
A-And so... who is this person?

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.090
Oh, this is my son, Nagomu.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.840
I'm sorry to ask you, 
but would you say hello?

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.350
By "son"...

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.250
You mean the person who 
you've barely heard from

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.570
since he abandoned the shop and left?

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.100
Oh, stop it, would you?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.740
You're embarrassing me!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.910
I am Yukihira Itsuka.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:08.060
I've been allowed to stay here 
for free for about a year now.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.810
Stop talking like we're strangers!

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:13.320
Everyone here thinks of 
you as our girl, you know?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.790
Nagomu, she's my successor.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.260
He's just saying that without 
thinking it through.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.740
What's that?

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.550
She's still only ten years old!

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.170
Ma'am, I am here with that intent.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.180
I'm not giving this place up to 
someone so selfish he'd just run off.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.680
Well said!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.920
That's exactly what makes you a 
successor I can put my trust in!

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.870
May I go to work now?

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.820
Yes. We'll be counting on you again today!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.360
Work?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.490
Yes. After school, she helps us in the shop.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.060
At this point, she's the face of our shop.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.040
<i>She moves well, working tirelessly.</i>

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.770
<i>I see. He wasn't lying when he 
said she's the face of the shop.</i>

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:10.920
I'm sorry.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.440
All of our seats are non-smoking.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.830
Huh? Come on. One smoke after 
a meal's no big deal, right?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.180
It bothers the other customers.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.760
You sound pretty arrogant 
for being just a kid.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.330
Just go away. It's not like 
you'd understand anyway.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.930
And you don't seem to understand 
in spite of your age.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:28.650
What?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.880
I may be a child, but I can call the police.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.530
Shall I to go crying to them saying 
you're obstructing our business?

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:39.560
Thank you for your patronage.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.440
Are you okay?

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.290
It's nothing.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:47.390
In situations like that, it might 
be better to ask an adult for help.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.510
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.050
Did something happen?

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.660
I see.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:04.060
She... You could say she isn't 
used to asking for help.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.070
She says she doesn't want to trouble us,

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.850
and tries to take care of everything herself.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.450
What about her parents?

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.570
Left her behind, alone, and went missing.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.090
That day, it was snowing 
heavily, which was unusual.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.390
Her mother had left them long before,

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.080
and it was just her and her father, 
who carried a guitar with him.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.420
Through a series of connections, 
they came to visit us here.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.000
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.000
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.050
The next day...

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.050
<b>To the nice man and lady from Ryokushou,</b>

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.050
<b>Please take care of this girl.</b>

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.050
<b>Sorry, Itsuka</b>

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.540
He left a letter with just a 
few words on it and disappeared.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.050
When I look at that girl behaving 
so bravely, it makes me feel sad.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:46.810
We said we'd look after her 
until she feels satisfied.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:51.660
Still, there's only so much we 
can do in place of her parents.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.430
We can't keep up with a child's world.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.320
I'd say she's more like 
a grandkid anyway, right?

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.510
That's it!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.250
If you're planning to stay here and train,

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.040
then won't you try to be 
like a parent for her?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:05.860
Huh?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:11.290
Since she doesn't feel the need to be 
restrained around you, she might open up!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.210
Me? A parent?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:18.090
<i>So that means... that was 
her looking for her dad?</i>

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.280
Oh, right. Your room.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.360
The storeroom's the only one available, 
so just use it however you like.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.770
What? Seriously?!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.040
Dinner's ready. Will you 
go call Nagomu for me?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.140
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.280
Um...

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.060
About dinner...

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.550
A guitar.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:16.120
Masa-san! Good morning.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.360
Saki-kun. Morning.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.510
The sun has started coming up earlier.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.700
And the air is fresh and light.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:28.640
Fifty-one...

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.210
Fifty-two...

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.960
<i>This scene is 180 degrees 
away from "fresh and light"!</i>

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.960
Fifty-three...

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.460
You've been working very hard 
since early this morning.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.520
You should be grateful that I'm 
letting you train here at all.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.460
That's right.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:46.050
Training starts early in the morning, 
so you'll need to sharpen up.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:49.430
Is doing 50 push-ups right after waking 
up really how wagashi artisans train?!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:54.190
Try imagining being a parent who has to 
give her over-30 son this kind of advice.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.190
Huh? What about my rice?

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.190
Please feel free to serve yourself.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.490
Understood.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.450
Yay, yay!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.450
I'm going to go sweep out front!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.700
Itsuka...

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.520
Make Nagomu do that. 
You go get ready for school.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.330
What?

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.810
Did you say something with 
that mouth? Did you?!

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:17.770
I don't want to.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:22.510
"The front of the shop is its face. 
Keeping it clean is important."

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.340
That's what you taught me, isn't it?

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.110
I don't want to entrust that to this person.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:27.110
I see. I see!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.000
In that case, you go to 
the storeroom and get

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.140
sugar, wasanbon, rice flour, 
glutinous rice flour...

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.870
Please don't tell me all at once.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.230
Can't you remember, you moron?!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.980
Man, this is heavy.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.990
That's right. Back when I was a kid...

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:47.030
I wanted to help, but I spilled it all.
 This reminds me of back then...

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.960
What's wrong? You seem upset.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.080
Grandpa!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.120
Here.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.580
Why don't you eat this?

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.040
Getting something in your stomach 
makes you feel better, right?

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.340
And eating something yummy will make 
you feel even better than that.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:07.080
That means our wagashi will make 
me feel better than anything else!

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:12.200
In that case, I'm going to have to ask 
you to take care of our Ryokushou for me.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.050
<i>Grandpa...</i>

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.560
<i>I wonder if my being here...</i>

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.990
<i>makes him happy.</i>

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.120
Bye! Stay safe!

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.460
Be careful!

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.700
I'm going now!

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.620
<i>I won't lose.</i>

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:40.000
I'm not giving this place up to 
someone so selfish he'd just run off.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.880
<i>He ran from the shop. 
He ran from making sweets.</i>

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:45.640
<i>He just did as he liked 
and abandoned his duties.</i>

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:50.470
<i>I won't lose to an irresponsible 
adult like him! Not ever!</i>

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.160
Mistress, I have to go soon.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:56.810
Oh, Otsurusan. It's already time for 
you to leave, isn't it? Thank you.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:57.930
Mistress...

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:00.620
"Where's the order log?" 
The master was asking about that.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.430
What? Honestly.

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.070
Isn't it where it usually is?

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:07.100
Nagomu, will you help in the 
shop for a little while?

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:08.660
Oh. Sure.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.180
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.290
<i>This one's Flowing...</i>

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.840
<i>Nightingale...</i>

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.080
<i>Budding Crimson.</i>

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.280
Each one's such a little beauty!

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:21.630
U-Um...

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.530
Is this it?

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.870
Yes, that's it.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.840
Oh no! I've left Nagomu in the shop!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.190
I'll switch with him!

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:31.430
Would you?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.840
I'll switch with—

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:38.880
Take care, okay? You're going
 to make them so happy!

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.560
Stop that! Nagomu!

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:43.690
I'm so sorry about this. Thank you!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.390
He went and did it, huh?

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:48.570
Yes. We could hear it perfectly 
all the way back here.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:55.770
Here.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.250
Grandfather's done with it, 
so I was told to give it to you.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:07.550
The sweets grandpa and the others make...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.220
They're really beautiful, you see?

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:13.640
And when they were making them, 
the sweets in their hands looked happy.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.050
It made me feel a ridiculous 
amount of empathy for the sweets.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:19.960
I loved them so much, I couldn't stand it.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:23.660
When they were sold, I'd just cry and cry.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.600
And then...

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.880
That's true.

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:32.440
The way things are, it might be better 
to have Nagomu go do something else.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.490
So...

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:45.930
I went to high school, and after meeting 
an upperclassman I really admired...

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:47.370
I started playing guitar.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.460
After that, my grandpa died.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.290
I sort of felt like I'd been left behind.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.880
That's right.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.820
I ran away, just like you said.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:03.990
Itsuka-chan!

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.900
Yes, this is her.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:11.640
What?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:14.860
A hundred mugwort jouyo manju?

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:18.160
They said they'd come to pick 
them up tomorrow evening.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.810
They said they were so impressed 
with the way Itsuka works

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:23.880
that they asked her to come to the 
phone so that they could praise her!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.760
That's impressive, getting an order like that!

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:30.330
Well, then, let's get everything 
ready for tomorrow.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:31.130
Yes, sir!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.680
Right. Let's get it done!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.590
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.590
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.430
The wonderful smell of mugwort!

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:41.500
Don't eat any.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.600
I'm not gonna eat them.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:48.890
Our jouyo manju use koshi an, smooth red 
bean paste. And they aren't too sweet.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:50.840
I'm back!

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.280
Welcome home!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.780
We just finished them up.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.390
I'll go change clothes!

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.290
I'm looking forward to seeing who's 
coming to pick them up, aren't you?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.670
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.670
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.750
Thank you very much!

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.780
Thank you very much!

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:15.970
Welcome!

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:18.550
There are two of us. Do you 
have any seats available?

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:21.000
I'll show you the way.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:26.600
They don't seem to be coming. 
Shall I give them a call?

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.980
If you wouldn't mind.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.140
I—

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:35.830
<i>The number you have dialed 
is not currently in service.</i>

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:40.990
<i>The number you have dialed 
is not currently in service.</i>

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.250
That might be a number 
from a disposable phone.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.790
You're saying it was a prank?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.290
A disposable phone?

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.560
What do you want to do? 
It's already closing time.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.550
Itsuka, don't worry about this.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.000
They thought of you as just a 
kid and decided to tease you.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:58.500
Itsuka!

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:02.140
I'll figure something out!

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:04.120
Figure something out? But you don't have to!

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.770
What is a child, on her own, 
going to be able to do?

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:09.310
There's no need to be so stubborn, is there?

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:12.030
I'm not being stubborn, 
I'm taking responsibility!

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.370
Fulfilling your responsibilities has nothing 
to do with being an adult or a child!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.340
Hey! Someone, go after her!

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:20.390
All right!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.150
Wait.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.220
I'll go.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:33.000
Would you like some manju?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:36.920
Ryokushou's manju is delicious!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:39.010
Would you like some?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:42.010
Would you like some manju?

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.460
It's delicious!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:53.720
<i>No one's stopping for me.</i>

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:03.030
<i>I have to be more reliable. Otherwise...</i>

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.780
Are you all right?

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:07.500
Huh?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.250
A child, alone, doing something like this...

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.110
Police officers are sure 
to come check on you.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:15.130
You should hurry up and go 
back to your mom and dad.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.260
Papa is...

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.850
I told you.

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:23.900
Kids only get in the way.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.510
They're a handful...

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:27.340
and they're no help with anything.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.830
What do I do?

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.270
I'm going to be a child no one needs again.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.030
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:46.340
A chestnut?

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:50.290
You did great, working so hard 
on your own. Very admirable.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:53.530
Now it's time to start the show!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.440
<i>Sweets are good for a tired body.</i>

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:03.100
<i>Together with a rest, a familiar sweetness.</i>

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:07.220
<i>One, with tax included, is 360 yen!</i>

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.220
<i>The aroma of mugwort will 
make you feel so calm.</i>

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:14.580
<i>Jouyo manju! We're having a special sale!</i>

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.880
What's that? Looks like fun!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.850
But wagashi isn't really...

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.680
You there, young lady!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:24.030
Anko is great for promoting beauty!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:28.220
<i>Adzuki beans have vegetable 
fiber and polyphenols.</i>

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.330
<i>And the thing women are often short of...</i>

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:33.340
<i>Iron! You can get a lot of that, too!</i>

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.240
<i>Plus, it's low in calories!</i>

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:39.420
I'll have some!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.630
Thanks!

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.110
Some for me too!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.560
What shop are you from?

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.150
We're from Ryokushou!

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.860
Can I have just one?

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.390
Of course you can!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.660
Thank you!

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:50.990
May I take a picture?

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:53.870
No problem! Make sure you promote us!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.400
Thank you!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.020
Five manju, please!

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:57.610
Right away!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.690
Thank you!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.910
Well, we managed to sell out somehow.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:15.230
Making mistakes is fine. My family 
considers you our girl, right?

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.250
You're still just a fledgling to me.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:19.710
Here.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.390
I swiped two and set 'em aside.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.010
That's 720 yen.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.160
You sure are a responsible heir, aren't you?

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.390
Oh, it's so good!

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.480
You know, when people eat yummy things,

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:39.940
it makes them feel better.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.530
Won't you try to be like a parent for her?

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.450
<i>I don't know about being something 
as important as that, but...</i>

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:52.900
<i>If I can help her, then...</i>

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:56.460
Huh? What is it?

00:21:56.460 --> 00:22:02.130
Nothing. Just... our manju are 
the yummiest ever, right?

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.140
Yes.

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:42.060
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:42.060
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:41.530
We're back!

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:44.280
What's with your head?!

00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.440
Oh. I've had it on this whole time.

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:48.740
I thought you did it on purpose.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:51.990
<i>Hello! This is Reon!</i>

00:23:50.070 --> 00:24:10.090
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:50.070 --> 00:24:10.090
<b>"Echoing Through the Hydrangea"</b>

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:53.740
<i>Please listen to my new song!</i>

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:55.720
Just one each, okay?

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:58.600
Reon does not exist!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:03.500
I felt like, through music, I'd be 
able to express all kinds of emotions.

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:05.770
Mitsuru-chan's music...

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:07.960
I really like it!
